            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"text\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"text\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "DOCUMENT_PROCESSOR"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "parser"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PARSER",
          "id": "1762333347214",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762333347216_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Task: You are a Document Extraction agent.\n\nDocument text: {{$context.$nodes.SCANNER.$output.text}}\nFields to extract (fieldsList): {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.fieldsList}}\n\nExtraction rules:\n- Extract only from the current document text and the current request context.\n- Do not use values from older, unrelated commands or prior records.\n\n- For each item in fieldsList:\n  - Use the exact \"name\" as the JSON key.\n  - If \"description\" is present and non-empty, use it as extraction guidance.\n  - If \"description\" is empty, extract the value that best matches the field name.\n\nValue handling rules:\n- Keep extracted values exactly as shown in the document EXCEPT:\n  \n  1) Date Fields:\n     - Any field representing a date (e.g., Date From, Date To, DOB, Issue Date, etc.)\n     - Convert to format: YYYY-MM-DD\n     - If conversion is not possible confidently, return null\n\n 2) Issuing Country:\n   - Extract the country name exactly as shown in the document.\n   - Populate:\n     • \"Issuing Country\" with the original country name (e.g., Japan)\n     • \"Issuing Country Code\" with the ISO 2-letter code (e.g., JP)\n   - If the ISO code cannot be determined confidently, set \"Issuing Country Code\" to null.\n   - If the country itself is not found, set both fields to null.\n\n- If a field cannot be found confidently, set its value to null.\n\nOutput rules:\n- Return exactly one valid JSON object.\n- Use only the fields from fieldsList as keys.\n- Do not include any any explanation, extra keys, text, or additional commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
      "errorHandlers": [
        {
          "type": "EMAIL",
